     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><font color=\"#000000\">@</font><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">joseph.l...@vanderbilt.edu</a>, @<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mhunt...@gmail.com</a>, @<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">patrick...@vanderbilt.edu</a>, and others:</div><div><br></div><font color=\"#000000\">Someone recently asked how to obtain the Nlsy97 links as a csv.  They spent a few minutes on our site and couldn&#39;t find it easily.  </font><div><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">I&#39;m posting two solutions below, but I&#39;m a little concerned they had difficulty.  I&#39;m open to a different organization or explanation on the site if it will help.  Or maybe there should be something on the site&#39;s front page.  However keep in mind that there are <a href=\"https://nlsy-links.github.io/NlsyLinks/reference/index.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://nlsy-links.github.io/NlsyLinks/reference/index.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792521438786000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3cOHCLYonSjmjnf5WoZjdH\">already six datasets</a>, and this should continue to grow.</font><div><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><font color=\"#0000ff\" size=\"4\">Short answer: </font></b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><font color=\"#000000\" style=\"font-size:11pt\">go to </font></span><a href=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nlsy-links/NlsyLinks/master/outside-data/nlsy-97/links-2017-97.csv\" style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nlsy-links/NlsyLinks/master/outside-data/nlsy-97/links-2017-97.csv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792521438786000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3O8A8-R9zTo3wyNRaOliFI\">https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nlsy-links/NlsyLinks/master/outside-data/nlsy-97/links-2017-97.csv</a><font color=\"#000000\"> </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font color=\"#000000\"> </font><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><font color=\"#0000ff\" size=\"4\">Longer answer: </font></b><font color=\"#000000\">go to the</font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"></p><ol><li><font color=\"#000000\"> main website (</font><a href=\"https://nlsy-links.github.io/NlsyLinks/\" style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://nlsy-links.github.io/NlsyLinks/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792521438786000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3acU8BMBwUlwxpfn18i5pK\">https://nlsy-links.github.io/NlsyLinks/</a><font color=\"#000000\">), then </font></li><li><font color=\"#000000\">“Datasets &amp; Functions” (</font><a href=\"https://nlsy-links.github.io/NlsyLinks/reference/index.html\" style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://nlsy-links.github.io/NlsyLinks/reference/index.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792521438786000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3cOHCLYonSjmjnf5WoZjdH\">https://nlsy-links.github.io/NlsyLinks/reference/index.html</a><font color=\"#000000\">),\r\nthen </font></li><li><font color=\"#000000\">one of the two 97 datasets (either, “Links97Pair” or “Links97PairExpanded”.  </font></li><li><font color=\"#000000\">Towards the bottom, each page has the\r\nfollowing section; click on “download the csv”.  Here&#39;s what it looks like on the page:</font></li></ol><p></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></p>\r\n\r\n<h2 style=\"margin:0in 0in 7.9pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(243,243,243)\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font size=\"4\">See also</font><span style=\"font-size:24pt\"><u></u><u></u></span></font></span></h2>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:7.9pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;box-sizing:border-box\"><strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(243,243,243)\"><font color=\"#000000\">Download CSV</font></span></strong><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,sans-serif\"><font color=\"#000000\" style=\"background-color:rgb(243,243,243)\"> If you&#39;re using the\r\nNlsyLinks package in R, the dataset automatically is available. To use it in a\r\ndifferent environment, <a href=\"https://github.com/nlsy-links/NlsyLinks/blob/master/outside-data/nlsy-79/links-2017-79.csv?raw=true\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/nlsy-links/NlsyLinks/blob/master/outside-data/nlsy-79/links-2017-79.csv?raw%3Dtrue&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792521438786000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1j8171wcgLMZFJRp5bbN0Q\">download the csv</a>,\r\nwhich is readable by all statistical software. <a href=\"https://github.com/nlsy-links/NlsyLinks/blob/master/outside-data/nlsy-97/links-metadata-2017-97.yml\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/nlsy-links/NlsyLinks/blob/master/outside-data/nlsy-97/links-metadata-2017-97.yml&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792521438786000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1oYRwLCVYD9e1km7N6e9LU\">links-metadata-2017-97.yml</a> documents\r\nthe dataset version information.</font><u></u><u></u></span></p></div></div></div>"
